   "properties": {
    "role": "aoi",
    "name": "Itapebi, Bahia: eucalyptus planting on pasture (synthetic restore demo site)",
    "synthetic": true,
    "planted": 2019,
    "source": "Synthetic demo site, not a documented project: no planting record with a public polygon could be reached from the build environment (USFS FACTS, Restor and others are blocked), so this site was located from independent public layers (GLAD annual tree canopy height 2015 to 2024, Hansen GFC v1.13, ESA WorldCover, Sentinel-2 imagery). A straight-edged block about 62 ha, 3 km west of Itapebi in southern Bahia (UTM 24S): pasture through 2018, soil prepared in the July 2019 Sentinel-2 scene, young canopy by June 2020; GLAD canopy height is 0 on 99 percent of its pixels through 2020 and 5 m or more on 99 percent in 2021 (mean 6.3 m), 19 m by 2024. Uniform heights and the block outline say it is a plantation (likely eucalyptus), so it stands in for a tree planting, not an ecological restoration. No Hansen loss 2015 to 2025. The 1 to 3 km ring is 84 percent open pasture that stayed open.",
    "land_use": "plantation (likely eucalyptus) on former pasture",
    "area_ha": 62.0
